<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Three moments, not one</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A trade fair is often reduced to the stand. In fact it is decided in three moments: beforehand, when invitations go out and the right visitors need a reason to come. In the aisle, where it is decided in seconds whether someone stops. And afterwards, when a conversation is meant to become an order.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Design only for the middle moment, and you get a beautiful stand and little follow-up business.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">The stand is the most visible tool — rarely the most effective.</p>
</section>

<!-- 02 — WHAT IS CREATED -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
